\"en-c21-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>global differences in consumption</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>sustainable agriculture</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>digital technology and food</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1},{"id":"en-c21-t2-l-g3-3","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 27-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the flow-chart below.</p><p>Choose FOUR answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-F, next to Questions 27-30.</p><p>Student project: developing a new food product</p><p>Initial aim</p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span></p><p>Literature review</p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span></p><p>Product development</p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span></p><p>Product production</p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span></p></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--inline\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This was challenging but enjoyable.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This led to some disagreement.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This was easy to decide on.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This was helped by the guidelines provided.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This seemed like an unnecessary stage.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This involved selecting a new ingredient.</span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-2-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c21-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3178715-cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-2-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c21-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p>Challenges facing the cruise ship industry</p><p>Problems with overtourism</p><p>• <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> is one of the worst problems.</p><p>• A tourist <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> is being introduced in some cities to reduce numbers, e.g. Barcelona.</p><p>• Bruges: action was taken to limit day trips from the nearby port because the city was becoming a 'theme park' (e.g. many shops were only stocking <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and souvenirs).</p><p>• Dubrovnik: limits the number of tourists by managing the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of cruise ship arrivals.</p><p>Problems of perception</p><p>• Cruises are generally associated with the elderly.</p><p>• There is an assumption about the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of cruises.</p><p>• People think there may be too many <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><p>Solutions</p><p>Cruise lines are attracting younger customers by:</p><p>• becoming more sustainable e.g. using hybrid engines.</p><p>• having a wide range of activities e.g. boxing, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and well-being programmes.</p><p>• offering a diverse selection of food including <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> options.</p><p>• providing reliable <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><p>• improving marketing on social media with high quality <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-2-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c21-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-c21-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c21-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"13th January/13 January/January 13/January 13th/13.01/13.1","correct_answer_variants":["13th January","13 January","January 13","January 13th","13.01","13.1"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3178418_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c21-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-c21-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c21-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"48","correct_answer_v